{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_api_base_effect_baseeffect", "label": "BaseEffect", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/api/base-effect.md", "source_location": "lines 1-4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_base_effect_getconfig", "label": "getConfig(): BaseEffectConfig", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api/base-effect.md", "source_location": "Abstract / overridable", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "outputNode is invoked exactly once when the pass is registered; every later frame updates only the .value of the UniformNodes passed in uniforms (setUniform), so the node graph is never rebuilt."}, {"id": "docs_api_base_effect_builtin_state", "label": "Built-in runtime state (uTime / uMouse / width / height)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api/base-effect.md", "source_location": "\u7d44\u307f\u8fbc\u307f\u306e\u5b9f\u884c\u6642\u72b6\u614b", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The owner updates these through an internal API immediately before update()/resize(), so subclasses cannot break them by forgetting super.update()/super.resize()."}, {"id": "docs_api_base_effect_no_resolution_uniform", "label": "No resolution uniform (use TSL screenSize)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/api/base-effect.md", "source_location": "\u89e3\u50cf\u5ea6 uniform \u306f\u7528\u610f\u3057\u3066\u3044\u306a\u3044", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "screenSize auto-updates every render with no dummy value or wiring, but it reports the currently bound RenderTarget's size; width/height exist only for the JS-side real numbers TSL cannot supply, e.g. new THREE.RenderTarget(w, h)."}, {"id": "docs_api_base_effect_feedback_buffer", "label": "BaseEffect feedback buffer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api/base-effect.md", "source_location": "\u30d5\u30a3\u30fc\u30c9\u30d0\u30c3\u30af\u30d0\u30c3\u30d5\u30a1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "BaseEffect owns the ping-pong RenderTarget pair, first clear, per-frame draw and swap, resize and disposal so a subclass only writes the accumulation formula. The buffer lives off-screen and is not automatically in the post chain, so nothing appears until outputNode composites feedbackTexture with inputTexture."}, {"id": "docs_api_base_effect_feedback_halffloat", "label": "HalfFloat default for feedback buffers", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/api/base-effect.md", "source_location": "\u65e2\u5b9a\u304c HalfFloat \u306a\u7406\u7531", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "At 8-bit, 10/255 multiplied by 0.95 rounds back to 10/255, so a decaying trail never fades and leaves a ghost; repeated-decay effects need HalfFloat or better."}, {"id": "docs_api_base_effect_feedback_node_timing", "label": "feedback.node evaluation timing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/api/base-effect.md", "source_location": "feedback.node warning", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The accumulation buffer is drawn before the composer's render() (right after update()), so inputTexture at that moment points at last frame's about-to-be-overwritten ping-pong target and is meaningless; mixing in the previous pass must happen in outputNode instead. Uniforms changed inside update() are reflected immediately."}, {"id": "docs_api_base_effect_helpers", "label": "BaseEffect helpers (setUniform / getUniform / getPass / enabled)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api/base-effect.md", "source_location": "Helpers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_base_effect_setupgui", "label": "setupGUI(gui) hook", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api/base-effect.md", "source_location": "setupGUI", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_base_effect_effectcomposer", "label": "EffectComposer / EffectPass (low-level)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api/base-effect.md", "source_location": "EffectComposer / EffectPass", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_api_base_effect_baseeffect", "target": "docs_api_base_effect_getconfig", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/api/base-effect.md", "source_location": "Abstract / overridable", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_api_base_effect_baseeffect", "target": "docs_api_base_effect_builtin_state", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/api/base-effect.md", "source_location": "\u7d44\u307f\u8fbc\u307f\u306e\u5b9f\u884c\u6642\u72b6\u614b", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_api_base_effect_builtin_state", "target": "docs_api_base_effect_no_resolution_uniform", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/api/base-effect.md", "source_location": "\u89e3\u50cf\u5ea6 uniform \u306f\u7528\u610f\u3057\u3066\u3044\u306a\u3044", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_api_base_effect_getconfig", "target": "docs_api_base_effect_feedback_buffer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/api/base-effect.md", "source_location": "BaseEffectConfig.feedback", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_api_base_effect_feedback_halffloat", "target": "docs_api_base_effect_feedback_buffer", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/api/base-effect.md", "source_location": "\u65e2\u5b9a\u304c HalfFloat \u306a\u7406\u7531", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "